IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- what Part 6 Division 2 (ss 205 to 209B) and the Thirteenth Schedule share. LAYER 1 (the law, objectively).
--
-- Two small helpers and one type, used by the modules of this part (sgc2-s205-appointment, sgc2-s205aa-resignation,
-- sgc2-s205a-exemption, sgc2-s206-208a-duties, sgc2-s209-interpretation). Names begin "s 205" (the first section of the
-- Division) because that is the label of the provision whose pattern they carry; they define no rule of their own.
--
-- THE PATTERN FOR A DUTY WITH A LAST DAY. Where the text says a person "must, within N days after X, do Y", a decision
-- function is "in default": TRUE where the act was done after the last day, or has not been done and the day as at which the
-- question is asked is after the last day; FALSE otherwise (done in time, or time still running). The last day comes from
-- the keel's period: functions, never from date arithmetic of our own.
-- An act done on any day up to and including the last day is in time, an act before the event's window included (fork line F-P2 in NOTES.md).

§ `What the offences of this Division share`

-- The persons the Division makes guilty again and again: "the company and every director of the company who is in default"
-- (ss 205(17), 205A(3), 205AC(4), 205AD(5), 205AF(5), 206(2)). Declared once, here, under the first of them.
DECLARE `s 205(17) person charged` IS ONE OF
    `s 205(17) the company`
    `s 205(17) a director of the company who is in default`
    `s 205(17) any other person`

§ `Default in doing an act by a last day`

-- Plain BOOLEAN helper: the act was done after the last day, or has not been done and the last day has passed.
-- The day the act was done is read only where the act has been done (a placeholder otherwise).
GIVEN `the act has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the act was done` IS A DATE
      `the last day for the act` IS A DATE
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 205 helper: default in an act due by the last day` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN `the day the act was done` GREATER THAN `the last day for the act`
    ELSE `the day as at which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the last day for the act`

-- The number of days from one day to a later one, for the WITHIN of a regulative rule (the trace clock counts days from the event).
GIVEN `the day of the event` IS A DATE
      `the last day for the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 205 helper: the days from the event to the last day` MEANS
    (Day `the last day for the act`) MINUS (Day `the day of the event`)
